  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_036 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.715 acc / 0.687 F1. The largest gains came from ViT-L over ResNet50 (+8.3%) and multi-profile over single-profile. Fusion strategy evidence is weak: concat marginally beat weighted with ResNet50 (0.527 vs 0.523, ~0.4% gap, within noise). Question: Does the fusion strategy (concat vs weighted) interact differently with the much stronger ViT-L image features? This experiment changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other dimensions at their empirically best values (scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, multiprofile). Why best use of budget: It is a minimal, clean one-variable test that directly reduces uncertainty about whether fusion is an important design axis under the strongest image encoder. If weighted outperforms concat here, it opens a new optimization direction; if not, it confirms concat is sufficient and we can focus remaining budget on untested dimensions (e.g., scgpt RNA encoder or transformer aggregation with ViT-L)."
}

